Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:34:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6: the Coupons row is
 read only when its list loaded, and its verdict holds through the run (OR-04)

The rendered Coupons page is read as one of three states (coupon_list_reading): cards drawn (loaded), a
stated count of 0 without the loading indicator (loaded and empty), or not loaded (the site's loading
indicator, no count, or a count without cards), which proves no coupon absent. The route keeps every answer
with its reading and fetch; a page not loaded is asked again after the listings, within coupons_attempts
answers for the run (4 by default, coupons_retry_wait_s apart), across restarts.

The plan names the Coupons row as a route of the run. A run whose plan names it is complete only when the
route is READ: collection_complete (the dataset label) and G3 require it; the listings alone still decide
what is carried forward (listings_complete). The coverage file's row 0 states the route's verdict (COMPLETE
or NOT_READ, with why and the number of answers) instead of "not in this run's scope", and the manifest
states it under routes.

A product's own page rendered but still showing the loading indicator and no coupon row is read as
"loading": its coupons are unread (unread_loading, DIGITAL_TERMS_UNREAD), not absent and not in conflict
with the card; a tile's coupon stays unknown.
